      <div type="clause" n="19">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIAs">II As</ref> 19</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="19" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="160" ed="#liebermann"/>Ond we cwædon be þeowan men, gif he fúl wurþe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_19.lnote.oe.1-2"/> æt þam ordale, þæt mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_19.lnote.oe.2"/> gulde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_19.lnote.oe.1-2"/> þæt ceapgild ⁊ swinge hine (man<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_19.lnote.oe.3"/>) ðriwa oððe þæt oþer gild sealde; ⁊ sy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IIAs_19.lnote.oe.4"/> þæt wite be healfum wurðe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_19.lnote.oe.1-2"/> æt þam ðeowum.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IIAs_19.lnote.oe.5"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="19" corresp="#wit-ld"><pb n="160" ed="#liebermann"/>Be ðeowman<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_19.lnote.oe.1"/> ðe ful wurþe æt ordale. We cwædon be ðeowmen, gif he ful wyrþe æt þæm ordale, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> mon gylde þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ceapgylde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_19.lnote.oe.1"/> ⁊ swynge hine ðrywa oþþe þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> oþer gylde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_19.lnote.oe.1"/> sylle; ⁊ sy þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> wite be healfan wyrþe æt ðæm ðeowan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="19" corresp="#wit-ot"><pb n="160" ed="#liebermann"/>. . we cwædon be þeowan men, gif . . ful wyrþe æt þam ordale, þæt man g:lde þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ceapgyld ⁊ swing . . . hine þriwa oððe þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> oþer g:ld sealde; . . . þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> wite be healfu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> wyrþe æt þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> ðeowan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="19" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="161" ed="#liebermann"/>De seruo qui reus sit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_19.lnote.oe.1-3"/> ad ordalium. Diximus de seruo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_19.lnote.oe.2-2"/>, si<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_19.lnote.oe.3-2"/> reus sit in ordalio, reddatur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IIAs_19.lnote.oe.4-2"/> captale simpliciter<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IIAs_19.lnote.oe.5-2"/>, et uerberetur seruus ipse<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IIAs_19.lnote.oe.6"/> ter, aut secundam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IIAs_19.lnote.oe.7"/> redditionem addat; et sit wita<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IIAs_19.lnote.oe.8"/> dimidia<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IIAs_19.lnote.oe.9"/> de seruo.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" n="19" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="136" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be ðeowman ðe ful wurþe æt ordale.]<ptr type="editorNote" n="10" target="#IIAs_19.attnote.fn.10"/> Ond we cwædon be þeowan men<ptr type="editorNote" n="11" target="#IIAs_19.attnote.fn.11"/>, gif he fúl wurþe<ptr type="editorNote" n="12" target="#IIAs_19.attnote.fn.12"/> æt þam ordale, þæt mon gulde<ptr type="editorNote" n="13" target="#IIAs_19.attnote.fn.13"/> þæt ceapgild<ptr type="editorNote" n="14" target="#IIAs_19.attnote.fn.14"/> ⁊ swinge hine man ðriwa oððe þæt oþer gild<ptr type="editorNote" n="15" target="#IIAs_19.attnote.fn.15"/> sealde<ptr type="editorNote" n="16" target="#IIAs_19.attnote.fn.16"/>: ⁊ sy þæt wite be healfum wurðe<ptr type="editorNote" n="17" target="#IIAs_19.attnote.fn.17"/> æt þam ðeowum<ptr type="editorNote" n="18" target="#IIAs_19.attnote.fn.18"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="161" ed="#liebermann"/>(Vom Sklaven, der beim Ordal überführt wird. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi>) Und wir bestimmten, über den unfreien Mann, wenn er überführt wird beim Ordal, dass man [der Herr<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_19.lnote.de.1"/> dem Kläger] das Ersatzgeld zahle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_19.lnote.de.2"/>, und jener dreimal gegeisselt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_19.lnote.de.3"/> oder das zweite<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IIAs_19.lnote.de.4"/> Ersatzgeld gezahlt werde; und das Strafgeld vom Unfreien sei halb so viel werth [wie vom Freien].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">(Of the slave who is convicted at the ordeal. Ld) And we determined concerning the unfree man, if he is convicted at the ordeal, that [the lord] pay [the plaintiff] the compensation-money, and that he be flogged three times or the second compensation-money be paid; and that the fine for the unfree be worth half as much [as for the free].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="137" ed="#attenborough"/>And we have declared with regard to a slave who has been found guilty in the ordeal<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_19.attnote.n.1"/>, that [his master] shall pay the amount involved, and either inflict three scourgings on him or pay a second sum equal to the amount involved. And the fine for theft by a slave shall be half the amount [paid by a freeman for a similar offence].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="421" ed="#whitelock"/>And we have pronounced with regard to a slave, that, if he is convicted at the ordeal, the price of the goods is to be paid, and he is to be flogged three times or the price is to be paid a second time. And the fine is to be at a half-rate where slaves are concerned.</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_19.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">160</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_19.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">160</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">u <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">u on an erasure</seg></note>
